is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: spine_router_0_1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: FRR BGP neighbor configuration on spine_router_0_1. The eBGP session to leaf_router_0_1 is misconfigured.

Mechanism: BGP OPEN messages are rejected when the remote AS in the neighbor stanza doesn’t match the AS carried by the peer. On spine_router_0_1, neighbor 172.16.0.11 is configured with remote-as 65999, while leaf_router_0_1 actually runs AS 65201. This AS mismatch causes the session to cycle and remain in Idle/Active, matching the reported “OPEN rejected by spine with an AS error.”

Localization: The problem is on the spine_router_0_1 ↔ leaf_router_0_1 link (spine eth2 172.16.0.10/31 to leaf eth1 172.16.0.11/31). Evidence:
- spine_router_0_1 running-config: “neighbor 172.16.0.11 remote-as 65999.”
- leaf_router_0_1 BGP: local AS 65201; neighbor 172.16.0.10 remote-as 65101.
- BGP summaries: spine shows 172.16.0.11 in Idle; leaf shows 172.16.0.10 in Idle. All other peers on both devices are Established, and routing continues via the other spine, explaining minimal user impact.

Root cause: A bad config push set the spine’s neighbor 172.16.0.11 remote-as to 65999 instead of the leaf’s actual AS 65201.

Corrective fix: On spine_router_0_1, change “neighbor 172.16.0.11 remote-as 65999” to “neighbor 172.16.0.11 remote-as 65201” and commit; the session should Establish and advertise prefixes normally. Verify with “show ip bgp summary.” === END ===